<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rawa Voivodeship</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1462–1793</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Rawa Voivodeship was a province of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-poland">Kingdom of Poland</a> and later the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a>, created in 1462 when the Masovian duchy of Rawa was incorporated into the Crown. Its seat was Rawa Mazowiecka, and it comprised the lands of Rawa, Sochaczew and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gostynin">Gostynin</a>. It belonged to the Greater <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> Province of the Crown until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-partition-of-poland">Second Partition of Poland</a> in 1793 gave it to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rawa-voivodeship.jpg" alt="Rawa Voivodeship" width="320" height="280" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Poznaniak · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:RON_wojew%C3%B3dztwo_rawskie_map.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
